| Solve: TubeSearch's JavaScript helper (tscli solve), started by
| !TubeSearch as a task of its own when YouTube's TV app addresses need
| their challenges answered (%0: the job file, %1: the answer file).
| Its memory, up to about 110 MB the first time a new YouTube player is
| met, is a dynamic area of its own ("TubeSearch Solver"), freed when it
| ends. The program itself needs this much of the slot:
WimpSlot -min 3072K -max 3072K
Run <TubeSearch$Dir>.tscli -wimp solve %0 %1
